d "q-167677" :question/problem "$\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{5\\text{i}}=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $5\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+5\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-5\\text{i},$ or simply $-5\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-5\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{5\\text{i}} & =\\frac{5+2\\text{i}}{5\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-5\\text{i}}{-5\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-25\\text{i}-10{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-25{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-25\\text{i}-10(-1)}{-25(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{10-25\\text{i}}{25}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{10-25\\text{i}}{25} & =\\frac{10}{25}-\\frac{25}{25}\\text{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}-\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-167677/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-167677"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316885/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "b81daf5f-e51c-51d3-bfaf-983a1184bc78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316885/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2d45df6c-3419-51e4-b80f-354626e3acba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316885/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer-field/choices ["q-316885/field-1/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316885/field-2/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "da14f780-82e1-5dfa-9aa8-4516f3fb928c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316885/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "2cb2c6d4-24e6-5409-8036-856ee45b04e0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316885/field-2/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer-field/choices ["q-316885/field-2/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316885" :question/id #uuid "5fd3fcca-a299-5ed3-acd7-f31b57fee4ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-316885" :question/problem "Evaluate the expression below, expressing your answer in the form $a+b\\text{i},$ where $a$ and $b$ are real numbers.\n\n$\\frac{-4+9\\text{i}}{6\\text{i}}=($\n{{field-1}} \n$)\\,+\\,($\n{{field-2}}\n$)\\,\\text{i}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $6\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+6\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-6\\text{i},$ or simply $-6\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-6\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-4+9\\text{i}}{6\\text{i}} & =\\frac{-4+9\\text{i}}{6\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-6\\text{i}}{-6\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{24\\text{i}-54{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-36{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{24\\text{i}-54(-1)}{-36(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{54+24\\text{i}}{36}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{54+24\\text{i}}{36} & =\\frac{54}{36}+\\frac{24}{36}\\text{i} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{2})+(\\frac{2}{3})\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316885/field-1" "q-316885/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "730fc9a7-a1b8-55a4-b8d3-666f87b82958"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316885"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
